.TH ABDNS 1 "November 2026" "abdns 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
abdns \- control abdnsd, the encrypted DNS client of this computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B abdns
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abdns
talks to
.BR abdnsd (8)
over its local control socket. abdnsd sends every DNS query of the computer to your own
DNS-over-HTTPS resolver first, then to encrypted fallbacks in the configured order, and uses the
network's DNS only as a last resort, for example to sign in to a captive portal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Mode (encrypted or network DNS), servers and which one answers, network, names sent in clear.
Readable by every user.
.TP
.B test
Query every server now and print its response time. Exits with status 1 if one fails.
.TP
.BR mode " " auto | encrypted | local
Force a mode. \fBencrypted\fR forbids the network DNS; \fBlocal\fR forces it (stubborn captive
portal); \fBauto\fR lets abdnsd decide. Administrators only.
.TP
.B reload
Read the configuration file again now. abdnsd also notices changes by itself within 5 seconds.
Administrators only.
.TP
.B check
Validate the configuration file and list the servers in order, like \fBsshd \-t\fR.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \-f "] [" \-n
.IR lines ]
Show the service log; \fB\-f\fR follows it.
.TP
.BR token " [" \fIserver\fR ]
Store the secret path segment of a server's DoH URL in that server's \fBtoken_file\fR (mode
0600). Reads one line from standard input: the token alone or the full URL. In a terminal, the
input is not echoed. If abdnsd is running, it is asked to reload and uses the token at once. As
root.
.TP
.BR install " / " uninstall
Install and start, or stop and remove, abdnsd as a launchd service when no package manager does
it (macOS and Linux, as root). \fBuninstall\fR also restores the network DNS.
.TP
.BR completions " " bash | zsh | fish
Print a shell completion script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Configuration file. Default: the first that exists of
.IR /etc/abdns/config.toml ,
.IR /opt/homebrew/etc/abdns/config.toml ,
.IR /usr/local/etc/abdns/config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for \fBstatus\fR and \fBtest\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/abdns/config.toml
Configuration, see
.BR abdnsd (8).
.TP
.I /var/run/abdns/status.json
Current state, readable by every user.
.TP
.I /var/log/abdns/clear.log
Every name sent in clear.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR abdnsd (8)
